# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values. NEVER commit .env.

# ── Database (PostgreSQL) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create a free PostgreSQL database at https://neon.tech (recommended for
# Vercel) and paste its connection string here. Use the POOLED connection
# string (the one containing "-pooler") — Vercel's serverless functions open
# many short-lived connections and will exhaust a direct connection otherwise.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/DATABASE?sslmode=require"

# ── Auth.js ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate with:  openssl rand -base64 32   (or https://generate-secret.vercel.app/32)
AUTH_SECRET=""
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=""
# The site's public URL. http://localhost:3000 in dev; your real domain in prod.
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ── Seed accounts (used only by `npm run db:seed`) ───────────────────────────
# These bootstrap the first Admin/EIC and Editor accounts. After seeding, the
# admin can create more editors and change any account's email/password from
# Dashboard → Users, so these are starting values, not permanent fixtures.
SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL="eic@marsu.edu.ph"
SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=""
SEED_EDITOR_EMAIL="editor@marsu.edu.ph"
SEED_EDITOR_PASSWORD=""

# ── Password-reset email (Forgot Password) ───────────────────────────────────
# Without these two, login still works but "Forgot Password?" emails are never
# sent. Setup (see src/server/email.ts for details):
#   1. On the Gmail account, turn on 2-Step Verification.
#   2. Google Account → Security → 2-Step Verification → App passwords →
#      create one for "Mail". Google shows a 16-character password.
#   3. Paste it below with spaces removed. This is NOT the normal Gmail password.
GMAIL_USER="thematrixtoday.msc@gmail.com"
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=""

# ── File uploads (Vercel Blob) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# From Vercel: Storage → Blob → create a store → copy the read-write token.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=""
